arm64: fence an IRQ unmask only when a deadline waits for it

Patch 0010 exits after every local IRQ enable and restore so that a clockevent
deadline deferred under PSTATE.I is asserted at an exact instruction. Most
unmasks have no deferred deadline, and those exits only cost time. Userspace
now sets the page's irq_pending word at the exit where it defers a due
deadline and clears it once the deadline is delivered or disarmed. The page
changes only at exits, so the guest's read after the unmask sees the same
value on every run, and the fence exits at the same instruction the
unconditional fence did whenever a deadline is waiting. Until the page is
validated, every unmask still exits.

This patch is Linux-kernel code (GPL-2.0), carried as a diff under the Harmony
repository's designated guest-kernel patch exception.

---
--- a/drivers/clocksource/harmony_arm_pvclock.c
+++ b/drivers/clocksource/harmony_arm_pvclock.c
@@ -51,6 +51,7 @@ struct harmony_arm_pvclock_page {
 	__le64 guest_clock_hz;
 	__le32 flags;
 	__le32 vcpu_index;
+	__le32 irq_pending;
 } __packed;
 
 /* Set once registration has validated the page; guards reads before its
@@ -215,14 +216,20 @@ void harmony_arm_virtual_time_tick(void)
 }
 
 /*
- * Expose the exact instruction boundary after Linux unmasks IRQs without
- * assigning an execution-density tick. Userspace gives this ordinary exit
- * only the paravirtual-exit quantum.
+ * Expose the exact instruction boundary after Linux unmasks IRQs, but only
+ * while userspace holds a due deadline for it: it sets irq_pending at the exit
+ * where it defers the deadline under PSTATE.I and clears it after delivery.
+ * The page only changes at exits, so the check is exact. Before the page is
+ * validated every unmask exits. Userspace gives this exit only the
+ * paravirtual-exit quantum.
  */
 void harmony_arm_irq_unmask_fence(void)
 {
 	if (!harmony_registers)
 		return;
+	if (READ_ONCE(harmony_pvclock_ready) &&
+	    !le32_to_cpu(READ_ONCE(harmony_page()->irq_pending)))
+		return;
 	writel(1, harmony_registers + HARMONY_IRQ_UNMASK_FENCE);
 }
 
